Looking at this question: "supply cost by product" refers to the supplies model, which is at the grain of one row per supply and product combination. There's no metric for supply cost, so I need to use the column ref with an aggregation.

The grouping should be by product identity (entity:supplies.product_id — the key on the supplies model itself, since that's the same model as the measure), with supply_name as display... but wait, checking Rule 1: display must belong to the SAME entity as the key. Here the key is product_id (product entity), and the natural label for a product is product_name (on the products model), not supply_name (a finer-grained thing that would multiply rows). Since supply_cost lives at the supply grain, grouping by product_id and displaying supply_name would multiply rows per Rule 1's warning. I'll group by product_id only, without a mismatched display.

